r 2024, an estimated 1,630,874 Syrians have returned.","href":"https://data.unhcr.org/en/documents/download/122248"},{"text":"Breakdwon by Country of Return [chart labels:] Türkiye 639,995 Lebanon 630,697 Jordan 284,881 Iraq 41,179 Egypt 27,970","href":"https://data.unhcr.org/en/documents/download/122248"},{"text":"Following hostilities in March 2026, assistance was temporarily suspended and later resumed under a force-majeure framework before regular voluntary repatriation activities restarted on 1 July 2026.","href":"https://data.unhcr.org/en/documents/download/124199"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"},{"key":"today","kind":"researched","text":"Lebanon's statistics office surveyed 39,000 households and estimated 4.842 million residents in mid-2018, not counting refugee camps, army barracks or informal settlements; 20% were not Lebanese citizens. The UN's 2018 figure is 5.98 million. The two are not directly comparable.","figure":{"value":4842000,"what":"people living in ordinary homes in Lebanon (excludes refugee camps, barracks and informal settlements), CAS/ILO household survey","date":"2018"},"unFigure":{"value":5984120,"what":"UN estimate for 1 July 2018","date":""},"gapPct":23.6,"verdict":"context","links":[{"label":"Central Administration of Statistics Lebanon and ILO, Labour Force and Household Living Conditions Survey 2018–2019 (copy on UNHCR's data portal), Dec 2019","href":"https://data.unhcr.org/en/documents/download/73718"}],"quotes":[{"text":"The population of Lebanon for mid-2018 was estimated at around 4.842 million people, excluding people living in non-residential units, such as army barracks, refugee camps and adjacent gatherings, and informal settlements. Eighty per cent of residents are Lebanese and 20 per cent are citizens of other countries.","href":"https://data.unhcr.org/en/documents/download/73718"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"}],"links":{"self":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/countries/LBN.json","countries":"https://fertility-track